Highlights:
The bundler worker is a web worker responsible for compiling and bundling Svelte code in the browser for the REPL and Tutorial systems. It orchestrates Rollup bundling, Svelte compilation, npm package resolution, and optional Tailwind CSS processing entirely client-side without server dependencies.
For npm package resolution details, see [NPM Package Resolution](https://deepwiki.com/sveltejs/svelte.dev/4.3-navigation-system). For the execution environment that runs the bundled code, see [Code Execution Environment](#4.4). For the UI layer that invokes the bundler, see [REPL UI and State Management](https://deepwiki.com/sveltejs/svelte.dev/4.1-design-system-and-tokens).
...
The bundler worker operates as a dedicated web worker thread that receives file data and bundling options via message passing, then performs compilation and returns the bundled JavaScript code.
...
The worker responds to two primary message types defined in the `message` event listener:
|Message Type|Purpose|Handler|
|`init`|Load Svelte compiler version|`get\_svelte()`|
|`bundle`|Compile and bundle files|`bundle()`|
The worker maintains a `current\_id` variable to handle concurrent bundle requests, aborting outdated operations when a new request arrives.
...
The bundler creates a virtual file system using a `Map<string, File>` called `lookup` that contains user files plus four synthetic files:
...
The `repl\_plugin` is the heart of the bundler, implementing Rollup's `resolveId`, `load`, and `transform` hooks:
|Hook|Responsibility|
|`resolveId`|Maps import specifiers to absolute URLs (virtual, npm, or http)|
|`load`|Retrieves file contents from virtual files, npm packages, or URLs|
|`transform`|Compiles `.svelte`, `.svelte.js`, and `.svelte.ts` files|
...
## Module Resolution Logic
The `repl\_plugin.resolveId` hook implements sophisticated module resolution:
...
The resolved IDs use URL-like namespaces:
* `virtual:///\_\_entry.js` - Virtual files created by the bundler
* `npm://$/@scope/package@1.2.3/path/to/file.js` - npm packages fetched from registry
* `https://example.com/file.js` - External URLs imported directly
...
## Svelte Compilation Pipeline
The `transform` hook in `repl\_plugin` compiles Svelte components using the Svelte compiler:
...
## Bundle Output Generation
After Rollup completes, the bundler generates output in IIFE format:
...
output includes:
|Field|Type|Description|
|`uid`|number|Request identifier for deduplication|
|`client`|object|Generated JavaScript and source map for client execution|
|`server`|object|Server-side rendered output (currently disabled)|
