   - the host imports the project's own `vite` from the workspace's node_modules and calls `createServer({ configFile, plugins: [cawcoStage()], server: { hmr: { overlay: false } } })`;
   - start on first use or open; `ready` within 60 s or `error`; health every 15 s; restart ×3 with backoff, then `error`; asleep after 30 min with no viewer and no agent read; wake on open; stop on archive;
   - the stage's port is shown through the existing `port:<port>@<workspace>` preview source.

   Vite toolchains only in this slice: SvelteKit, Svelte, React, Vue, Solid and Preact. Astro, Nuxt and Next come in a later item. Any other toolchain is answered by name, per spec §10 and the owner's decision: those projects show components as an HTML `page` artifact on the project's CSS. The tool's refusal says exactly that.
